share new arXiv features directly on our website.\nL152: \nL153: Both individuals and organizations that work with arXivLabs have embraced and accepted our values of openness, community, excellence, and user data privacy. arXiv is committed to these values and only works with partners that adhere to them.\nL154: Have an idea for a project that will add value for arXiv's community? cite44†Learn more about arXivLabs†info.arxiv.org .\nL155: \nL156: cite45†Which authors of this paper are endorsers? | Disable MathJax (cite46†What is MathJax?†info.arxiv.org )\nL157: \nL158: We gratefully acknowledge support from our major funders, cite47†member institutions†info.arxiv.org , , and all contributors.\nL159: cite48†About†info.arxiv.org · cite49†Help†info.arxiv.org · cite50†Contact†info.arxiv.org · cite51†Subscribe†info.arxiv.org · cite52†Copyright†info.arxiv.org · cite53†Privacy†info.arxiv.org · cite54†Accessibility†info.arxiv.org · cite55†Operational Status (opens in new tab)†status.arxiv.org L160: \nL161: Major funding support from\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nIntroducing shopping research in ChatGPT | OpenAI (https://openai.com/index/chatgpt-shopping-research/)\nciteturn1916view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://openai.com/index/chatgpt-shopping-research/\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 214\nL0: cite0†Skip to main content L1: \nL2:   * [Button: Research]\nL3:   * [Button: Products]\nL4:   * [Button: Business]\nL5:   * [Button: Developers]\nL6:   * [Button: Company]\nL7:   * cite1†Foundation(opens in a new window)†openaifoundation.org L8: \nL9: cite2†Try ChatGPT(opens in a new window)†chatgpt.com [Button: Login]\nL10: \nL11: OpenAI\nL12: \nL13: November 24, 2025\nL14: \nL15: cite3†Product cite4†Company L16: # Introducing shopping research in ChatGPT\nL17: \nL18: A new shopping experience that helps you find the right products for you.\nL19: \nL20: cite5†Try in ChatGPT(opens in a new window)†chatgpt.com L21: \nL22: Loading…\nL23: \nL24: Share\nL25: \nL26: Finding the right products\nL27: \nL28:   * cite6†Finding the right products L29:   * cite7†How to use it L30:     * cite8†Describe what you need L31:     * cite9†Guide the research L32:     * cite10†Receive a personalized buyer’s guide L33:   * cite11†How it works L34:   * cite12†Transparency and trust L35:   * cite13†Limitations L36:   * cite14†Just the start L37:   * cite6†Finding the right products L38:   * cite7†How to use it L39:     * cite8†Describe what you need L40:     * cite9†Guide the research L41:     * cite10†Receive a personalized buyer’s guide L42:   * cite11†How it works L43:   * cite12†Transparency and trust L44:   * cite13†Limitations L45:   * cite14†Just the start L46: Today, we’re introducing shopping research, a new experience in ChatGPT that does the research for you to help you find the right products. Instead of sifting through dozens of sites, you can just describe what you’re looking for—“Find the quietest cordless stick vacuum for a small apartment,” “Help me choose between these three bikes,” or “I need a gift for my four year old niece who loves art”—and shopping research builds a thoughtful guide to help you decide.\nL47: It asks smart clarifying questions, researches deeply across the internet, reviews quality sources, and builds on ChatGPT’s understanding of you from past conversations and your ChatGPT memory to deliver a personalized buyer’s guide in minutes.\nL48: Shopping research is starting to roll out today on mobile and web for logged-in ChatGPT users on Free, Go, Plus, and Pro plans. To help with holiday shopping, we’re making nearly unlimited usage available to all plans through the holidays.\nL49: ## Finding the right products\nL50: \nL51: Hundreds of millions of people use ChatGPT to find, understand, and compare products. They want help making sense of the options and deciding what fits their needs, budget, and preferences.\nL52: Shopping research is built for that deeper kind of decision-making. It turns product discovery into a conversation: asking smart questions to understand what you care about, pulling accurate, up-to-date details from high-quality sources, and bringing options back to you to refine the results. It performs especially well in detail-heavy categories like electronics, beauty, home and garden, kitchen and appliances, and sports and outdoor.\nL53: For simple shopping questions like checking a price or confirming a feature, a regular ChatGPT response is quick and all you need. But when you want depth—comparisons, constraints, tradeoffs—shopping research takes a few minutes to give you a more detailed, well-researched answer.\nL54: ##\nL55: \nL56: ## Discovering new products\nL57: \nL58: Help me find a powerful new laptop suitable for gaming under $1000 with a screen that’s over 15 inches\nL59: \nL60: cite15†_{Try it now}⁠(opens in a new window)†chatgpt.com L61: \nL62: ## Finding lookalikes\nL63: \nL64: I’m looking for a dress that looks like this, but is full length and less than $250\nL65: \nL66: cite16†_{Try it now}⁠(opens in a new window)†chatgpt.com L67: ## Comparing items side by side\nL68: \nL69: I need a stroller. Something lightweight, compact, and easy to fold. Comfy for my toddler (good recline and canopy), can handle city sidewalks and some rougher terrain, and fit a mid to slightly-premium budget.\nL70: \nL71: Please compare these three models and share the best fit and trade-offs.\nL72: \n"
